#ROOMS
#39000
Sydney Opera House~
Broad curves lift above the Opera House's `waudience seats`x, drawing the eye
away from the close ranks of upholstery toward the height of the hall. Fine
wooden ribs make a warmer pattern within the larger shell. The armrests shine
more brightly than the backs, polished by waiting hands. Even in the hush, the
room seems built around the possibility of one clear note reaching everyone at
once.`x
~
0 36 1
B 1
G 69 27 400 100 0
T 3000
M 100 H 0
W ~
P
audience seats~
The seats face the performance space in close rows. Fabric softens the small
sounds of settling in, while worn armrests mark where earlier audiences have
waited, watched, and leaned toward their companions.`x
~
S
#39001
~
Two broad planes meet at an awkward angle on the near side, with muted green
paint picked out along the join. The floor carries a faint rectangular
outline, clearer at one end than the other. The open floor makes the slightest
unevenness conspicuous, a landscape of small seams and shallow shadows.`x
~
0 4 0
B 1
G 0 0 0 0 0
T 3000
M 100 H 0
W ~
S
